#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/hardware-detection.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "How Ditana probes your system at install time and adapts configurations transparently, with all detection logic centralized in one auditable file."
msgstr "Cómo Ditana examina el sistema durante la instalación y adapta las configuraciones de forma transparente, con toda la lógica de detección centralizada en un único archivo auditable."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/hardware-detection.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Hardware detection"
msgstr "Detección de hardware"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/hardware-detection.md
msgid ""
"A traditional installer offers you the same dialogs regardless of whether "
"your laptop has an Intel iGPU or an NVIDIA card; whether you're on bare "
"metal or in a VM; whether your CPU is affected by RETBleed or not. You're "
"expected to know."
msgstr ""
"Un instalador tradicional le ofrece los mismos diálogos independientemente "
"de si su computadora portátil tiene una iGPU de Intel o una tarjeta NVIDIA; "
"de si trabaja en hardware físico o en una VM; de si su CPU está afectada por "
"RETBleed o no. Se espera que usted lo sepa."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/hardware-detection.md
msgid ""
"Ditana adapts the dialogs to your hardware. Choices you don't need are "
"hidden or pre-filled with safe defaults; choices you do need surface with "
"sensible recommendations."
msgstr ""
"Ditana adapta los diálogos a su hardware. Las elecciones que no le hacen "
"falta se ocultan o se rellenan previamente con valores predeterminados "
"seguros; las que sí le hacen falta aparecen con recomendaciones sensatas."

#. type: Title ##
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/hardware-detection.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "The detection principle"
msgstr "El principio de detección"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/hardware-detection.md
msgid ""
"All probing that feeds the knowledge base lives in a single file: [`hardware-"
"detection.kdl`](https://github.com/acrion/ditana-config/blob/main/settings/"
"hardware-detection.kdl). Each detector is one line of Raku that runs once at "
"installer startup and exposes a value – usually a boolean – to the rest of "
"the knowledge base. Probing that needs more than a line lives in the "
"installer engine: the graphics card is matched against the lists NVIDIA "
"publishes, and the NVMe block format, rotational media and the EFI partition "
"are found there too."
msgstr ""
"Todo el sondeo que alimenta la base de conocimiento está en un único "
"archivo: [`hardware-detection.kdl`](https://github.com/acrion/ditana-config/"
"blob/main/settings/hardware-detection.kdl). Cada detector es una línea de "
"Raku que se ejecuta una vez al iniciarse el instalador y expone un valor —"
"normalmente un booleano— al resto de la base de conocimiento. El sondeo que "
"necesita más de una línea está en el motor del instalador: allí se coteja la "
"tarjeta gráfica con las listas que publica NVIDIA, y allí también se "
"detectan el formato de bloque NVMe, los medios rotativos y la partición EFI."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/hardware-detection.md
msgid "A few representative examples from the live file:"
msgstr "Algunos ejemplos representativos del archivo actual:"

#. type: Fenced code block
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/hardware-detection.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"- name=\"uefi\" \\\n"
"  detect=\"'/sys/firmware/efi'.IO.e\"\n"
"\n"
"- name=\"intel-cpu\" \\\n"
"  detect=\"'/proc/cpuinfo'.IO.lines.first(* ~~ /vendor_id/).contains('GenuineIntel')\"\n"
"\n"
"- name=\"virtual-environment\" \\\n"
"  detect=\"run('systemd-detect-virt', '-q').exitcode eq 0\"\n"
"\n"
"- name=\"is-retbleed-vulnerable\" \\\n"
"  detect=\"given '/sys/devices/system/cpu/vulnerabilities/retbleed'.IO\n"
"            { .e && .slurp.chomp ne 'Not affected' }\"\n"
msgstr ""
"- name=\"uefi\" \\\n"
"  detect=\"'/sys/firmware/efi'.IO.e\"\n"
"\n"
"- name=\"intel-cpu\" \\\n"
"  detect=\"'/proc/cpuinfo'.IO.lines.first(* ~~ /vendor_id/).contains('GenuineIntel')\"\n"
"\n"
"- name=\"virtual-environment\" \\\n"
"  detect=\"run('systemd-detect-virt', '-q').exitcode eq 0\"\n"
"\n"
"- name=\"is-retbleed-vulnerable\" \\\n"
"  detect=\"given '/sys/devices/system/cpu/vulnerabilities/retbleed'.IO\n"
"            { .e && .slurp.chomp ne 'Not affected' }\"\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/hardware-detection.md
msgid ""
"Each one reads from `/sys/`, `/proc/`, or shells out to a standard tool — no "
"proprietary hardware abstraction layer, no opaque database. If you want to "
"know *what* Ditana detects and *how*, the answer fits on one screen and you "
"don't need to leave the file."
msgstr ""
"Cada uno lee de `/sys/` o `/proc/`, o recurre al shell para ejecutar una "
"herramienta estándar: sin capa propietaria de abstracción de hardware ni "
"base de datos opaca. Si quiere saber *qué* detecta Ditana y *cómo*, la "
"respuesta cabe en una pantalla y no necesita salir del archivo."

#. type: Title ##
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/hardware-detection.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "From detection to decision"
msgstr "De la detección a la decisión"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/hardware-detection.md
msgid ""
"Detectors don't act on their own. They expose values that other settings "
"reference in their `default-value` or `available` expressions. The chain is "
"always: **detect → decide → install**."
msgstr ""
"Los detectores no actúan por sí solos. Exponen valores a los que otras "
"opciones hacen referencia en sus expresiones `default-value` o `available`. "
"La cadena es siempre: **detectar → decidir → instalar**."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/hardware-detection.md
msgid ""
"A clean example is CPU vulnerability mitigation. Each kernel-reported "
"vulnerability (Spectre v2, Meltdown, MDS, TAA, MMIO Stale Data, L1TF, "
"RETBleed, SRSO, GDS, RFDS) has its own detector. The corresponding "
"mitigation setting then references that detector as its default:"
msgstr ""
"Un ejemplo claro es la mitigación de vulnerabilidades de la CPU. Cada "
"vulnerabilidad que notifica el kernel (Spectre v2, Meltdown, MDS, TAA, MMIO "
"Stale Data, L1TF, RETBleed, SRSO, GDS, RFDS) tiene su propio detector. La "
"opción de mitigación correspondiente hace referencia entonces a ese detector "
"como su valor predeterminado:"

#. type: Fenced code block
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/hardware-detection.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"- name=\"kernel-option-retbl\" \\\n"
"  dialog-name=\"CPU Vulnerability Mitigation Options\" \\\n"
"  short-description=\"Enforce Retbleed Mitigation (retbleed=auto,nosmt)\" \\\n"
"  default-value=\"`is-retbleed-vulnerable`\"\n"
msgstr ""
"- name=\"kernel-option-retbl\" \\\n"
"  dialog-name=\"CPU Vulnerability Mitigation Options\" \\\n"
"  short-description=\"Enforce Retbleed Mitigation (retbleed=auto,nosmt)\" \\\n"
"  default-value=\"`is-retbleed-vulnerable`\"\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/hardware-detection.md
msgid ""
"If your CPU isn't affected, the checkbox starts unchecked. If it is, it "
"starts checked. Nothing is filtered by CPU: every mitigation is listed "
"either way, so you can also see what your CPU was found not to need. The one "
"thing that does remove them from the dialog is choosing `mitigations=off`, "
"which makes each of them pointless — see [how settings depend on each other]"
"(/under-the-hood/settings-logic/). See the [CPU mitigations page](/under-the-"
"hood/mitigations/) for the full per-vulnerability rationale."
msgstr ""
"Si su CPU no está afectada, la casilla empieza desmarcada. Si lo está, "
"empieza marcada. Nada se filtra según la CPU: todas las mitigaciones "
"aparecen en la lista en ambos casos, así que también puede ver lo que se "
"determinó que su CPU no necesita. Lo único que sí las quita del diálogo es "
"elegir `mitigations=off`, con lo que ninguna de ellas tiene sentido; "
"consulte [cómo dependen las opciones unas de otras](/under-the-hood/settings-"
"logic/). Consulte la [página de mitigaciones de CPU](/under-the-hood/"
"mitigations/) para ver la justificación completa de cada vulnerabilidad."

#. type: Title ##
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/hardware-detection.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Case study: Wayland compatibility"
msgstr "Caso práctico: compatibilidad con Wayland"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/hardware-detection.md
msgid ""
"Some detection requires less obvious sources. Modern Wayland compositors "
"like Niri strictly need 3D hardware acceleration — software rendering "
"(llvmpipe, softpipe) is not enough; the compositor will crash or refuse to "
"start."
msgstr ""
"Algunas detecciones requieren fuentes menos evidentes. Los compositores "
"Wayland modernos como Niri necesitan estrictamente aceleración 3D por "
"hardware: el renderizado por software (llvmpipe, softpipe) no basta; el "
"compositor se cerrará inesperadamente o se negará a iniciarse."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/hardware-detection.md
msgid ""
"Rather than guess from the GPU vendor, Ditana asks the kernel which DRM "
"driver is actually active for the rendering device:"
msgstr ""
"En lugar de deducirlo del fabricante de la GPU, Ditana pregunta al kernel "
"qué controlador DRM está realmente activo para el dispositivo de renderizado:"

#. type: Fenced code block
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/hardware-detection.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"- name=\"has-wayland-compatible-gpu\" \\\n"
"  detect=\"given dir('/sys/class/drm').grep(*.basename.starts-with('renderD')).first\n"
"            { $_ ?? ($_ ~ '/device/driver').IO.resolve.basename\n"
"                    ~~ any(<amdgpu radeon i915 xe nvidia nouveau virtio-pci virtio_gpu>)\n"
"                  !! False }\"\n"
msgstr ""
"- name=\"has-wayland-compatible-gpu\" \\\n"
"  detect=\"given dir('/sys/class/drm').grep(*.basename.starts-with('renderD')).first\n"
"            { $_ ?? ($_ ~ '/device/driver').IO.resolve.basename\n"
"                    ~~ any(<amdgpu radeon i915 xe nvidia nouveau virtio-pci virtio_gpu>)\n"
"                  !! False }\"\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/hardware-detection.md
msgid ""
"If your system's driver isn't on this list — `vmwgfx` in VMware, `hyperv_fb` "
"in Hyper-V, `bochs-drm` in some QEMU setups — `has-wayland-compatible-gpu` "
"evaluates to `False`. The Niri option disappears from the desktop-"
"environment selection, and Ghostty (which needs OpenGL 4.3+, unavailable to "
"software rasterizers) becomes unavailable:"
msgstr ""
"Si el controlador de su sistema no está en esta lista —`vmwgfx` en VMware, "
"`hyperv_fb` en Hyper-V, `bochs-drm` en algunas configuraciones de QEMU—, "
"`has-wayland-compatible-gpu` se evalúa como `False`. La opción Niri "
"desaparece de la selección de entornos de escritorio, y Ghostty (que "
"necesita OpenGL 4.3 o posterior, algo que los rasterizadores por software no "
"ofrecen) deja de estar disponible:"

#. type: Fenced code block
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/hardware-detection.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"- name=\"install-ghostty\" \\\n"
"  available=\"`install-desktop-environment AND has-wayland-compatible-gpu`\"\n"
msgstr ""
"- name=\"install-ghostty\" \\\n"
"  available=\"`install-desktop-environment AND has-wayland-compatible-gpu`\"\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/hardware-detection.md
msgid ""
"One detector, multiple consumers. Adding a hardware-gated option later is "
"usually a single change in the consumer's `available` field — no detection "
"logic needs to be touched."
msgstr ""
"Un detector, varios consumidores. Agregar más adelante una opción "
"condicionada al hardware suele ser un único cambio en el campo `available` "
"del consumidor: no hace falta tocar ninguna lógica de detección."
